      "content": "It sounds like you're experiencing a lot of distress and disappointment in your relationships. It's difficult when you feel that you are a burden. Have you considered exploring different types of therapy, such as cognitive-behavioral therapy (CBT) or acceptance and commitment therapy (ACT)? These approaches can help people learn how to cope with such intense emotions and thoughts differently. Remember, even if it feels that way now, it doesn't define your worth or potential for change in the future. Additionally, having a support network you can rely on might also be beneficial. Even if it's not the same as your family or friends, there are people and groups out there that understand what you're going through.",
